From 4ee9a38f305d0e44624efdd45c5358d784852754 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: leave Lunal mode when a monster teleports the borg

Lunal mode makes the borg stair-scum: it ignores danger and preparedness
checks on the assumption that it stands on, or next to, a staircase.
borg_parse_aux() already tries to switch it off when a monster spell
moves the borg ("commands you to return." and similar), but that test
compares the start of the line while the game's line starts with the
monster's name, and every monster spell line is recognised earlier and
queued as a "SPELL_nnn" reaction before the test is reached.  So after
a teleport-to or teleport-away the borg stayed in Lunal mode, away from
the stairs, and kept making Lunal choices such as heading down to a
depth it is not prepared for.

Switch Lunal mode off where borg_update() handles the queued spell
reaction for teleport-to and teleport-away.  Self-engaged Lunal mode is
re-evaluated on the next dungeon think as before; Lunal mode set in
borg.txt stays off for the rest of the session.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#193.
---
 src/borg/borg-update.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-update.c b/src/borg/borg-update.c
index b5cafd02f..fa50b1c27 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-update.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-update.c
@@ -1985,6 +1985,15 @@ void borg_update(void)
             int spell = atoi(msg + 6);
             if (spell == RSF_TRAPS)
                 created_traps = true;
+
+            /* Teleport-to and teleport-away move the borg off his grid.
+             * If in Lunal mode better shut that off, he is not on the
+             * stairs anymore */
+            if ((spell == RSF_TELE_TO || spell == RSF_TELE_AWAY)
+                && borg.lunal_mode) {
+                borg.lunal_mode = false;
+                borg_note("# Disconnecting Lunal Mode due to monster spell.");
+            }
         }
 
         /* Handle "cackles evilly" */
